@startuml
autonumber
title Namespace-aware WES request flow
actor Client
participant "WES Gateway" as GW
collections "Loaded backend registry" as Config
database "Gateway metadata" as DB
participant "Selected Toil WES" as Toil

== Submission ==
Client -> GW : POST /wes/v1/{namespace}/runs\nMultipart fields and attachments
GW -> Config : Resolve registered namespace
alt Unknown namespace
  GW --> Client : 404 (no backend request)
else Registered namespace
  GW -> GW : Validate fields and attachment paths
  GW -> DB : Create durable SUBMITTING record\nnamespace + backend + gateway run ID
  GW -> Toil : POST /ga4gh/wes/v1/runs\nAdd reserved gateway tags
  Toil --> GW : Upstream run ID
  GW -> DB : Associate upstream ID
  GW --> Client : Gateway run ID
end
note over GW,DB
An ambiguous submission keeps its durable record.
An operator can reconcile using the reserved tags.
The gateway does not retry the submission.
end note

== Status, detail and cancellation ==
Client -> GW : Request with namespace and gateway run ID
GW -> DB : Resolve run within namespace
alt Run not owned by namespace
  GW --> Client : 404
else Owned run
  GW -> Toil : Forward to original backend using upstream run ID
  Toil --> GW : WES response
  GW -> DB : Record supported log/artifact references (on detail)
  GW --> Client : Gateway run ID; gateway artifact links where supported
end

== Listing ==
Client -> GW : GET /wes/v1/{namespace}/runs?page_size=...
GW -> DB : Page namespace-owned records in creation order
loop Each run with an upstream ID
  GW -> Toil : GET /runs/{upstream_id}/status
  Toil --> GW : State
end
GW --> Client : workflows + namespace-scoped next_page_token
@enduml
